VeridianOS: give the gperf lookup function internal linkage

GCC reported "no previous prototype for 'in_word_set'
[-Wmissing-prototypes]" (shape_to_id.gperf:80, in the generated
cursor/shape_to_id.c). gperf emits the lookup function without a storage
class and has no option to make it static, so it was an external symbol
with no declaration (kept out of the library's exports only by
-export-symbols-regex). A static declaration is added to the gperf
declarations section; the definition that follows then has internal
linkage, which is what the function is: it is used only by
cursor_shape_to_id() in the same file. <string.h> is included first for
size_t (gperf >= 3.1 declares len as size_t).

The build host has no gperf, and shape_to_id.c ships pre-generated
(gperf 3.3), so the same change is made to shape_to_id.c, with the
"#line N" references to the .gperf file after the insertion moved down by
the two added lines, exactly as gperf would emit them. The .gperf hunk
comes first so that shape_to_id.c ends up newer and make does not try to
regenerate it. No behaviour change.


